export anchor QueryNotebookStyle:
    number: 411
    screen: DatabaseConsole
    name: Query notebook
    idea: The console is a notebook of numbered cells, so a short prose heading explains the question, the SQL cell carries its own output table, a chart cell draws the answer and the history is a log cell of earlier runs.
    base: dark
    palette:
        page: #18161c, the page and the style sheet
        rail: #1f1c24, the table rail and the status bar
        cell: #24212a, cell bodies and secondary buttons
        code: #1a181f, the code area and fields
        output: #2b2732, cell output and inline code
        line: #3a3542, every border
        ink: #ece8f1, text
        muted: #aaa3b5, execution counts, column types and meta
        accent: #ffae6b, the active cell, Run cell, chart bars and keywords
        onAccent: #2d1503, text on the accent
        function: #9dc4ff, function names
        string: #b9e08e, string literals
        ok: #9fe0a8, Done and the idle kernel ring
        bad: #ff9d96, Error, on #33202a
    type:
        Three families. Prose headings in serif, Charter, Bitstream
        Charter, Sitka Text, Cambria, 28px at 600 with 16px prose. Chrome in
        Inter, Segoe UI Variable, Segoe UI, 15px at 1.55. Code in
        ui-monospace, JetBrains Mono, SF Mono, 14px at 1.65, and execution
        counts in 12px mono.
    layout:
        A top bar with an orange pause mark, Brightwork Data, Notebook
        overdue review and a round Kernel idle production-replica pill on
        the right. A toolbar holds Run cell in orange, Run all and a plus
        Cell. A 220px rail lists the tables in mono with tasks opened as a
        disclosure showing its columns and types. The main column, about
        940px wide, stacks cells with a 56px gutter for counts. First a
        borderless md cell with the serif title Overdue tasks by project and
        a sentence. Then cell 5, selected with an orange border and a 4px
        left bar, with a sql pill and ran at 09 41 in its header, the
        highlighted query, and an output table with index 0 to 2, project
        and open_overdue, ending in a green tick Done and 3 rows, 38 ms.
        Cell 6 is a chart cell with horizontal orange bars, labels on the
        left, values at the bar ends and dashed gridlines. A log cell lists
        the three runs with count, time, name and a tick Done or a triangle
        Error, the error shown as a red edged block. A status bar closes
        the screen. The style sheet is itself built from cells. Below 860px
        the rail moves on top, and on phones the counts sit above cells.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 14px between cells, 56px count gutter, 12 to 16px inside cells.
    density: Medium. One column of cells.
    corners: 12px cells, 8px buttons and fields, round kernel and language pills.
    borders: 1px #3a3542 around every cell. The active cell gets an orange border and a 4px inset left bar.
    shadows: None besides the inset left bar.
    icons:
        Few. Play, plus, a tick for Done, a triangle with a bang for Error
        and a ring for the idle kernel, each with its word.
    focus: A 2px orange outline offset 2px.
    tone: Analyst notes in sentence case, such as Run cell, ran at, Done and earlier runs today.
